---
import Slide from "../../components/Slide.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import raw_json from "../../img/web/raw_json.jpg"
import json_table from "../../img/web/json_table.jpg"
import bar_chart from "../../img/web/bar-chart.jpg"
import donut from "../../img/web/donut.jpg"
import d3_splash from "../../img/web/d3-splash.png"
---
<Slide t1="Data APIs">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Interactive APIs are generally referred to as AJAX</li>
        <li class="fragment">
            <span class="text-red-500">A</span>synchronous
            <span class="text-red-500">J</span>avaScript
            <span class="text-red-500">a</span>nd
            <span class="text-red-500">X</span>ML</li>
        <li class="fragment">(XML is rare; usually it's JSON or CSV)</li>
        <li class="fragment">React (JavaScript) can fetch data asynchronously: web request</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Development Stack">
    <p>This is what we currently have running:</p>

    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li>Astro development content server on port <code>4321</code>, serving out Astro pages,
            React components etc.&mdash;and also assets and data files (from the <code>public</code>
            folder)</li>
        <li>Flask development API server on port <code>5050</code>, serving out raw data
            in JSON or CSV format</li>
    </ul>

</Slide>

<Slide t2="Example JSON API">
    <p>Server side (port <code>5050</code>):</p>

    <div class="fragment text-sm-1">
        <CodeBlock lang="jsx" height="275px" lines="*|3|6-8"> { `
import random

@app.route("/json")
def json_start():
    return {
        "data" : [{"number" : x,
                   "square" : x * x,
                   "rand"   : random.randint(0, 100)} for x in range(100)]
    }
`.trim()
        } </CodeBlock>
    </div>

    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li class="fragment">Python dictionaries get converted to JSON over the wire</li>
        <li class="fragment">JSON being served at <code>http://localhost:5050/json</code></li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Browser Test">
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ raw_json }
            alt="Raw JSON"
            height="400"
            width="600" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="React Setup (Astro Hosted)">
    <div class="text-sm-2">
        <CodeBlock lang="jsx" height="550px" lines="*|7-9"> { `
import { useState } from 'react'

export default function JSONFetch() {
    const [state, setState] = useState([])      // List of records

    async function handleClick() {
        const response = await fetch("http://localhost:5050/json")
        const json = await response.json()
        setState(json.data)
    }

    return (
        <div>
            <h1>JSON Data Fetch</h1>

            <table>
                { state.map(
                    ({ number, square, rand }) => <tr key={ number }>
                        <td>{ number }</td>
                        <td>{ square }</td>
                        <td>{ rand }</td>
                    </tr>
                ) }
            </table>

            <button onClick={ handleClick }>
                Fetch data
            </button>
        </div>
    )
}`.trim()
        } </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="React Render">
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ json_table }
            alt="JSON in HTML Table"
            height="400"
            width="500" />
    </div>

    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li class="fragment">But: this won't work</li>
        <li class="fragment">Check browser console for errors</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t1="CORS">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">On server: need to enable CORS
            (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing)</li>
        <li class="fragment">Page service (Astro): <code>http://localhost:4321</code></li>
        <li class="fragment">API service (Flask): <code>http://localhost:5050</code></li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Enable CORS">
    <div class="text-sm-1 fragment">
        <CodeBlock lang="shell" height="100px">
            { `
%pip install flask-cors
            `.trim() }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
    
    <div class="text-sm-1 fragment">
        <CodeBlock lang="python" height="300px" lines="*|1,4">
            { `
from flask_cors import cross_origin

@app.route("/json")
@cross_origin(origin="*")
def json_start():
    return {
        "data" : [{"number" : x,
                   "square" : x * x,
                   "rand"   : random.randint(0, 100)} for x in range(100)]
    }
            `.trim() }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t1="D3">
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ d3_splash }
            alt="D3 Splash Page"
            height="600"
            width="800" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t1="D3">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Sophisticated data visualisation library</li>
        <li class="fragment">Like React: browser-based, JavaScript, dynamic page update</li>
        <li class="fragment">Can read and parse CSV files (or CSV streams from server)</li>
        <li class="fragment">Does not need server API (though of limited use without it)</li>
        <li class="fragment">For our purposes (for now): black box!
            <span class="text-black">&#x25FE;</span></li>
        <li class="fragment">(or a bento box &#127857;)</li>
        <li class="fragment">Install with: <code>npm install d3</code></li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="D3 Example 1">
    <ul><li class="fragment">Implemented as React component (<code>.jsx</code>)</li></ul>
    <ul><li class="fragment">Handout: <code>D3BarExample</code></li></ul>
    <ul><li class="fragment">Quiz: where is the data coming from?</li></ul>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center fragment">
        <Image
            src={ bar_chart }
            alt="Bar Chart"
            height="300"
            width="300" />
    </div>

    <ul><li class="fragment">Can you change the graph data?</li></ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Data Source">
    <ul>
        <ul>
            <li class="fragment">Data CSV: <code>7_OneCatOneNum_header.csv</code></li>
            <li class="fragment">Two-column: <code>Country</code> &times; <code>Value</code></li>
            <li class="fragment">Lives in <code>public</code> directory - served statically
                (or by Astro)</li>
        </ul>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="D3 Example 2">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Another "black box" example: donut chart</li>
        <li class="fragment">CSV data source will be Flask server using Pandas</li>
        <li class="fragment">Front end: D3 black box (<code>D3PopDonut</code>)</li>
        <li class="fragment">Not using React at all for rendering (but still updating DOM)</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t1="Pandas" t2="Data Manipulation Library">
    <ul><li class="fragment">Loads inside Flask; install with <code>pip</code></li></ul>

    <div class="fragment text-sm-1">
        <CodeBlock lang="shell" height="100px">
            { `
%pip install pandas
`.trim()
            }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Creating CSV Data">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">We can also create CSV data directly in Python</li>
        <li class="fragment">Pandas can turn Python structures into CSV</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="fragment text-sm-2">
        <CodeBlock lang="python" height="400px" lines="*|3|7-15|17-19">
            { `
import pandas as pd

@app.route("/pop-data")
@cross_origin(origin="*")
def pop_data():
    output = io.StringIO()
    my_data = [
        {"name": "<5", "value": 19912018},
        {"name": "5-9", "value": 20501982},
        {"name": "10-14", "value": 20679786},
        ...
        {"name": "75-79", "value": 7730129},
        {"name": "80-84", "value": 5811429},
        {"name": "≥85", "value": 5938752}
    ]

    df = pd.DataFrame(my_data)
    df.to_csv(output, index=False)
    return output.getvalue()
`.trim()
            }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="D3 Black Box">
    <div class="text-sm-2">
        <CodeBlock lang="javascript" height="350px">
            { `
const runD3donut = () => {
    d3.csv("http://localhost:5050/pop-data").then(data => {
        ...
        /* Lots of D3 and SVG cleverness... */
        ...
    }
}

export default function D3DonutExample() {
    useEffect(() => {
        runD3donut()
    }, [])

    return (
        <div id="my_dataviz">
        </div>
    )
}
`.trim()
            }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="D3 Donut">
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ donut }
            alt="D3 Donut Plot"
            height="500"
            width="500" />
    </div>
</Slide>
